    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch08-04--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch08-04: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.57";
    dc:description "The predicted arc is specific enough that a modest set of quadrant cells would confirm or refute it. Those cells are not available as an open morphometric dataset, though published figures show the qualitative anticlinal curve. The quantitative constants are only partly checkable from existing images.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: On quadrant-shaped flat cells, measure where the anticlinal wall meets the straight sides and what angle of arc it cuts off. An arc that meets both edges at right angles, cuts off about 55 degrees, and starts near three-tenths of the radius would support the claim; a straight radial wall or a periclinal wall in equal halves would refute it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Erythrotrichia discs and pressure-flattened frog or sea-urchin eggs are illustrated in classical plates, not in a public coordinate table.", "The numerical arc and radius fractions need measured outlines rather than schematic drawings.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.57"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch08-04--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of thompson1917-ch08-04 by Grok 4.7: 0.4";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
